## Pure ASCII, everywhere

Every file in this repository is ASCII-only -- code, config and Markdown alike. Write `--`, `->`,
`...`, `"` and `'`; never an em dash, arrow, ellipsis, curly quote, box-drawing character or emoji.
A non-ASCII character raises `UnicodeEncodeError` the moment a script prints it on a cp1252
console, breaks fixed-width output, and is invisible in review because it looks like its ASCII
neighbour. The rule has no exceptions because every exception has to be judged per character, by a
reader who cannot see the character.

```powershell
pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/quality/check-ascii.ps1          # report file:line:column and U+XXXX
pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/quality/check-ascii.ps1 -Fix     # rewrite the safe substitutions
```

