## Off limits

- Never read or write `<SECRET FILES / KEY PATHS / LOCAL DATA STORES>`. Secrets come from the
  environment, never from source, tests, or commit messages.
- Verify a dependency exists -- real, reputable, the name you intended -- **before** adding it, then
  add it to `<MANIFEST>` and re-lock. Never an ad-hoc install. Suggested package names are
  frequently hallucinated.
- Ask before anything irreversible or outward-facing: installs, migrations, file deletions,
  `git push`, force-push, `reset --hard`.

